  "id": "ffm",
  "term": "FFM",
  "definition": "FFM stands for the Fitness-Fatigue Model, a mathematical approach for using training data to predict exercise effects. It is used mainly in sports to support personalized evaluation and adjustment of training load based on an individual’s longitudinal data, although evidence for wider use in the general population is still limited.",
